WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.835
-Our next guest
is a talented actor you know

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:04.670
from his work in films
such as "Y tu mamá también,"

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:06.405
"The Motorcycle Diaries,"
and "Coco,"

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:09.175
and shows such as
"Mozart in the Jungle"
and "Station Eleven."

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:12.345
His latest project, "Cassandro,"
is available now on Prime Video.

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.579
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:15.815 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.684
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:21.087
[ Crowd chanting in Spanish ]

00:00:23.355 --> 00:00:25.058
-[ Speaking Spanish ]

00:00:27.626 --> 00:00:28.862
-[ Shouting Spanish ]

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.568 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.272 --> 00:00:41.940
[Chanting "Cassandro"]

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:45.010
Cassandro! Cassandro!

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:47.547
Cassandro! Cassandro!

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.817
-Please welcome back to the show
Gael García Bernal, everybody!

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.652
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.652 --> 00:01:06.899 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:09.168
Welcome back, Gael!
-Yes. Thank you so much.

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:12.105
It's so nice to be here again.
-This is a film about a world

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:13.773
I will admit
not knowing much about.

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:16.409
This is lucha libre wrestling.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.344
Tell us about exactly
what that means.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.146
-I'm surprised --
You never played that

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.447
with your friends, you know?

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:23.115
-We did, like, world wrestling,

00:01:23.115 --> 00:01:25.818
but not the sort of,
yes, the Mexican style.

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:27.320
-The Mexican style. Okay, okay.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.790
So it's, uh -- Lucha libre.
It's, uh, wrestling.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.859
Uh, the translation
is, like, "free wrestling."

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:35.861
So it's free.

00:01:35.861 --> 00:01:37.663
It's very much
you can do anything.

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:40.466
It's, uh --
It's got two ramifications

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:41.834
that are very specific.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.770
You know, like, sort of
the teams, you know?

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.706
It's técnicos, technicians,

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:50.309
and the rudos,
the rude ones, and --

00:01:50.309 --> 00:01:52.344
Or the rough ones. Sorry.
The rough ones.

00:01:52.344 --> 00:01:54.747
That would be the translation..
And, eh, it's the same.

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.382
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:59.319
And they, uh, you know --
there's many strands there,

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:01.488
where one of them
is the exoticos.

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:02.989
-Okay.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:06.826
-Which are, like, the campy,
uh, wrestlers, you know,

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:10.329
and, uh, Cassandro,
amongst his contemporaries --

00:02:10.329 --> 00:02:13.933
Cassandro is the character
I interpret in the film.

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.768
Uh, amongst his contemporaries,

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:18.370
they were the first ones
to subvert, more or less,

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:20.439
the notion that people
had about exoticos

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:23.309
because they came out,
uh, openly gay,

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:26.279
and, uh, people started
to support them

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:29.849
and people started to make them
want to win and, uh --

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.450
And, yeah. Yeah...

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:34.287
See the movie. See the movie.
See the movie.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:38.057
-So, Cassandro
is the wrestling name

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:40.860
of a real person called Saúl.
-Yes.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:43.863
-And, um, were you aware
of him growing up?

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:46.832
Was he sort of famous enough
to be on your radar?

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:48.901
-Well, he was -- He came
a little bit afterwards.

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:51.003
You know, as a kid,

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:55.241
I mean, I was watching,
uh, lucha libre on the TV,

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.577
and I saw many wrestlers

00:02:57.577 --> 00:03:00.546
like Atlantis, Octagon,
Rayo de Jalisco.

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:02.515
I mean, amazing,
like, legends, no?

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:04.216
Uh, and Cassandro
came a little bit after.

00:03:04.216 --> 00:03:05.618
You know,
because there's a point

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.753
where you get a little bit
embarrassed of watching the...

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:09.021
-Yeah, yeah.
-Yeah?

00:03:09.021 --> 00:03:12.625
So, uh, yeah. Cassandro came
a little bit afterwards.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:15.194
-You did get to meet
the real Cassandro.

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:16.529
-Of course!
-Uh, there you are.

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.398
-Yeah, man.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:19.598
Yeah.

00:03:19.598 --> 00:03:21.533
-He must have been, uh --

00:03:21.533 --> 00:03:23.269
I would imagine
he was so excited

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:25.004
that you were
all taking the time

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.472
to tell a story like this.

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:28.340
-He was very excited, yeah,

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:31.610
and, you know, just delighted
that we would also take on

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:35.715
the fact that, you know,
Saúl created Cassandro,

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:38.917
created this character
in order to find himself,

00:03:38.917 --> 00:03:41.086
you know, in order
to see all the dimensions

00:03:41.086 --> 00:03:43.255
of who he could be.

00:03:43.255 --> 00:03:46.525
And that led him in the road
to discovery, you know?

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:49.495
He was very happy,
I think, of what we did --

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:53.065
is that we also created
our own Cassandro,

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:58.137
and, uh, it took me on a path
of discovery, as well.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:00.172
And I think you can
tell that in the movie.

00:04:00.172 --> 00:04:02.742
It has that kind of, like --
that kind of, you know,

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:05.444
just a lot of nirvana moments,
you know,

00:04:05.444 --> 00:04:06.845
of fascination.

00:04:06.845 --> 00:04:09.648
And also allowed me
to play a luchador,

00:04:09.648 --> 00:04:11.817
you know, that as a kid,
I used to trash my room

00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:13.185
with my friends and my brother.

00:04:13.185 --> 00:04:14.787
You know, we used to --
And, uh --

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:16.889
And now I was doing it for real
in the ring.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:19.192
-He probably appreciated not
just that you told his story,

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:20.693
but you --
you took it seriously.

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:22.528
You tried to
get into wrestling shape.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.097
Is this accurate?
-Yeah.

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:25.964
-Did you enjoy the training?

00:04:25.964 --> 00:04:28.000
-I enjoyed -- Okay.
So, at the beginning, it was --

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.336
[ Laughter ]
-Thank you for your honesty.

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.605
We all know where this is going.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.774
-Everything -- Like all stories,
it begins well.

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:37.310
-Yeah.
-It begins me eating a lot

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.744
and gaining a lot of weight

00:04:38.744 --> 00:04:42.381
and, you know, doing a lot of,
uh, strength exercises,

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:44.884
you know, calisthenics
and those kind of things.

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:48.787
And then -- then two months
before starting to shoot,

00:04:48.787 --> 00:04:50.756
I started to do
the wrestling training.

00:04:50.756 --> 00:04:53.392
-Yeah.
-And that, uh -- Ah.

00:04:53.392 --> 00:04:56.262
That's just like --

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:58.298
I mean, as a warmup,
for example,

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:01.934
you have to do
100, like, dead falls

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.702
to the ground,
you know, like "tlack!"

00:05:03.702 --> 00:05:05.905
Yes? Yes. Oh-ho. Yeah?

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:07.940
Yeah, because you have to learn
how to fall.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.676
-Right.
-You know? And, uh --

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:12.244
And that's just to begin with,
and that's just the warmup.

00:05:12.244 --> 00:05:14.880
And if you were like one minute
late, they would come --

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.050
All the wrestlers
that you're training with,

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:19.251
they would come
and rush towards you

00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:20.820
and hit you as hard as you can,

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.289
and you had to fall
and go back again on top.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.057
And then another person.
Dah! Dah-dah!

00:05:25.057 --> 00:05:27.426
And obviously all of them
are bigger than me.

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:28.927
And, you know, it was like...

00:05:28.927 --> 00:05:30.963
-And nobody at any point
stepped in and said,

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:34.266
"This is the star of the movie.

00:05:34.266 --> 00:05:36.235
You leave this poor man alone."

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:39.238
-Oh. I think in the wrestling
world and in Mexico,

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:41.807
you would say that,
they would hit me even more.

00:05:41.807 --> 00:05:44.210
You know what I'm saying?
So it's like, "No, no.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:46.579
He's just train--
He's just training here."

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:48.948
-Did you do -- Was there
anything you had to do,

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:51.350
any sort of physical stunt
where you thought to yourself --

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.318
Because I'm older than you,
but not by a lot.

00:05:53.318 --> 00:05:55.521
And there are certain things
I do now where I think,

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:56.922
"Oh, I wasn't ready for that."

00:05:56.922 --> 00:05:58.924
Was there any moment
where you were like,

00:05:58.924 --> 00:06:00.826
"What am I doing here?"
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:06:00.826 --> 00:06:03.629
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
But the good thing is that --

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:05.597
I mean, we shot this
with our own --

00:06:05.597 --> 00:06:07.633
with our film family, you know?

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:10.135
So, the stunt coordinator
is called Balo Bucio,

00:06:10.135 --> 00:06:11.804
and he's fantastic.

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:16.442
And he was the interlocutor
with a wrestling organization

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:18.010
that we worked with, which is...

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:20.279
And they were really kind
and very giving.

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:23.583
And they -- From the beginning,
they were like,

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:25.584
"No, you can do this.
You can do this."

00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:29.155
And I was like, "I --
No, I can't. I can't do that."

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:30.456
They were like,
"Yeah, you'll manage.

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:31.790
You'll manage to do this."

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:33.792
And indeed I managed

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:37.662
to do all of the stunts
except one -- except two.

00:06:37.662 --> 00:06:40.299
But one very, very clear,

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:41.968
which is called
the Cassandro Bomb.

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:43.602
-Okay.
-Not even Cassandro

00:06:43.602 --> 00:06:45.371
is allowed to do it
because it's illegal, you know?

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:46.672
So it's like --
-What is --

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:48.273
Now you have to explain it.

00:06:48.273 --> 00:06:50.109
What's an illegal
Cassandro Bomb?

00:06:50.109 --> 00:06:53.312
-Oh, man. I, um -- I'd have to
show it, but then...

00:06:53.312 --> 00:06:54.947
-No, no, no.

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:58.050
-There wouldn't be a witness
to talk about it like that.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:00.552
-We're like,
"We're sorry Gael died,

00:07:00.552 --> 00:07:01.954
um, but do see his movie."

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:03.856
Hey. Thanks for being here.
It is a really special film.

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:05.357
And it's so nice
to see you again.

00:07:05.357 --> 00:07:07.293
-Thank you so much.
-Gael García Bernal, everybody.

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:09.128
"Cassandro" is streaming now
on Prime Video.

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:11.531
Stick around. We'll be right
back with more "Late Night."

